#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Plain-English rewrites of 18 early blog posts, November 2026.

The originals (written before the post kit existed) read as inflated filler:
"the engineered tranche strategy", "a tapestry of micro-markets", unsourced
median prices and rate forecasts. They also sit on the site's highest-value
topics. These versions keep every URL, drop the statistics and forecasts, and
follow the same content rules as the other post modules: explain how lending
works, never quote interest rates, never promise an approval.

The five Auckland area pages are in legacy_rewrite_posts_b.py.

Run:  python3 generate_local_intent_blogs.py legacy_rewrite_posts
"""

